# Build output

The app you run is always:

`C:\repos\TYViewer\x64\Debug\TYViewer.exe`

That folder is the Debug x64 runtime directory (exe, pdb, `glfw3.dll`, `res\`, `config.cfg`). Release x64 goes to `C:\repos\TYViewer\x64\Release\TYViewer.exe`.

Do not build or run `C:\repos\TYViewer\TYViewer\x64\`. That path is not an output directory. Object files, tlogs, and a second exe used to land there when `TYViewer.vcxproj` was built by itself.

Compile the solution, Debug|x64:

```
msbuild C:\repos\TYViewer\TYViewer.sln /p:Configuration=Debug /p:Platform=x64
```

`OutDir` is `$(ProjectDir)..\$(Platform)\$(Configuration)\`. `IntDir` is `TYViewer\obj\$(Platform)\$(Configuration)\`. Both are set in `TYViewer.vcxproj`, so a direct project build still writes the exe to `C:\repos\TYViewer\x64\Debug\`.
